# Node-only tooling. Pushing these breaks the GAS project at parse time:
# 'require is not defined' fires before ANY function runs, so every diag and
# every form dies. tools-deadscan.js did exactly that on 2026-08-13.
tools-*.node
# .node is Node's NATIVE-BINARY extension and cannot be require()d as JS.
# Node-only tooling uses .cjs instead, still excluded from the GAS push.
tools-*.cjs
